al; Escape closes it)","then":"while the modal is open keyboard focus is inside the modal (off the chip), and after Escape the modal is gone and keyboard focus is back on that same citation chip","when":"the chip is activated so the citation modal opens, and the modal is then closed with Escape"},{"given":"the citation modal is open and the element that had focus before it opened has since been removed from the document","id":"AC-4","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (unmount cleanup)","then":"closing completes without throwing and focus is not forced onto a detached node (document.activeElement falls back to the browser default, body) — the AC's 'when it remains in the document' conditional, pinned so a naive restore cannot regress it","when":"the modal closes"},{"given":"the citation modal is open and keyboard focus is on its Close button (the entry position this change introduces)","id":"AC-5","kind":"guard","seam":"app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)","then":"the modal closes via the existing document keydown handler (onClose invoked) — Escape behaviour is unchanged by the new focus management","when":"Escape is pressed"}],"dependencies":[],"invariants":["Focus entry and return are implemented entirely within CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle (refs plus one mount effect with cleanup); no new props, callbacks or state are added to CitationModal's callers, and ChatArea's conditional mount of CitationModal (ChatArea.tsx:787-789) is unchanged.","The focus effect uses an empty dependency array and does not re-run when the onClose prop identity changes (ChatArea passes a fresh closure every render); re-running on identity churn would re-capture the wrong opener mid-session.","Existing CitationModal tests that pin Escape close, backdrop close, close-button close, iframe embed src with start/autoplay, the 'Open on YouTube' link href and t param, transcript excerpt rendering with pre-wrap, the Video-unavailable states and body-scroll lock remain green without modification.","Dynamous citations never open the modal (ChatArea routes them directly to lesson_url or the missing-link toast), so neither focus criterion ever applies to them.","The Close (×) button keeps rendering unconditionally in every modal state (including Video-unavailable), since focus entry targets it as the only always-present control.","No focus trap, no inert/aria-hidden on background content and no new npm dependency; Tab may still travel from the modal to background content (accepted residual gap, not an acceptance criterion).","Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25 messages per user per 24 hours limit are untouched."],"issue":{"number":189,"title":"Citation inspection [keyboard]"},"out_of_scope":["Tab containment / focus trap, inert or aria-hidden on background content, and any focus-trap library (the issue forbids new external dependencies and containment is not an acceptance criterion).","The Dynamous citation path (direct lesson_url open and missing-link toast, issue #247).","New content sources, sharing, auth changes, factory authority changes and external dependencies (issue statement).","Modal visual design, video playback, timestamp links and the existing Escape / close-button / backdrop close semantics — preserved behaviour, not redesigned.","Authentication, owner-private conversations and the 25-messages-per-user-per-24-hours limit.","Backend, RAG pipeline and deployment files."],"risks":["React StrictMode (main.tsx) double-invokes effects mount→cleanup→mount in dev; the single empty-deps effect must capture the opener, focus the Close button, and restore in its own cleanup so the simulated remount re-captures the correct opener.","onClose identity churn: ChatArea passes a new closure every render, so keying the focus effect on onClose would re-capture document.activeElement mid-session (the Close button) and corrupt focus-return; reviewers should check the deps array specifically.","jsdom focus semantics: fireEvent.click does not move focus in jsdom, so checkpoints must establish focus with explicit element.focus(); a RED expectation declared from a click-based assumption will not match actual output.","Streaming re-renders can unmount the opener chip while the modal is open, making focus-return no-op to body — this is inside the AC's conditional, not a defect, and is pinned by the opener-removed guard.","Focus entry targets the Close button, which is only correct while it renders unconditionally; today it does, including the Video-unavailable states, and nothing in this build changes that.","Formatter gate: the kernel applies biome format on declared files; keep the new effect's style consistent with AddVideoModal.tsx's focus-on-open effect to avoid burning the hand-back on formatting."],"summary":"Add keyboard focus management to CitationModal: opening the modal moves keyboard focus to the modal's Close button (a usable control inside the dialog), and closing it returns keyboard focus to the element that opened it when that element remains in the document. Implemented entirely within CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle; no changes to callers, close paths, video playback, timestamp links or citation routing.","version":"2.0"},"sha256":"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b","source":"task-contract.json"},"design":{"content":{"ac_mapping":{"AC-1":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)"],"AC-2":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)"],"AC-3":["app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)"],"AC-4":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)"],"AC-5":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)"]},"allowed_new_files":[],"context_sha256":"674a06476636c493cb59dc93f93505743dff5b622665f990f3e4107dcff7d7fd","contract_sha256":"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b","data_flows":["citation chip (native <button> in Message.tsx) -> ChatArea.handleCitationClick -> setSelectedCitation -> CitationModal mounts (ChatArea.tsx:787-789)","document.activeElement at mount -> CitationModal mount effect -> opener captured in effect-local variable, focus moved to Close button ref","Escape keydown / Close button click / backdrop click -> onClose -> CitationModal unmounts -> effect cleanup focuses opener when opener.isConnected, else no-op (focus falls back to body)"],"invariants":["Opening the modal moves keyboard focus to the Close button (role button, accessible name 'Close') inside the role='dialog' element labelled 'Video citation'.","Closing via any path (Escape, Close button, backdrop click) restores focus to the element focused immediately before the modal opened, when that element remains in the document; when it does not, closing completes without throwing and activeElement falls back to the browser default (body).","The focus effect uses an empty dependency array; it never re-runs on onClose identity churn (ChatArea passes a fresh closure every render).","Existing close paths, the document keydown Escape handler, iframe embed src with start/autoplay, the 'Open on YouTube' link, transcript pre-wrap rendering, Video-unavailable states and the body-scroll lock are unchanged.","The Close button keeps rendering unconditionally in every modal state (including Video-unavailable) since focus entry targets it as the only always-present control.","No new props, callbacks, state or npm dependencies for CitationModal or its callers; no focus trap, no inert/aria-hidden on background content; ChatArea.tsx and Message.tsx are not modified.","Dynamous citations never open the modal, so focus entry/return never applies to them.","Focus management survives React StrictMode's dev double-invoke (mount→cleanup→mount re-captures the correct opener) because opener capture, Close-button focus and restore all live in one empty-deps effect invocation paired with its own cleanup."],"modules":["CitationModal (app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx)"],"planned_files":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx"],"public_interfaces":["CitationModal(props: { citation: Citation; onClose: () => void }) -> JSX.Element (signature unchanged; focus management is internal)"],"seams":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (mount effect with cleanup: focus entry + focus return)","app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx#CitationModal (document keydown Escape handler)","app/frontend/src/components/ChatArea.tsx#handleCitationClick (chip activation opens CitationModal; Escape closes it)"],"version":"1.0"},"sha256":"b12a6976956859c6e8671faf313c3183da72f643b7badf40fad1b106dbbacd02","source":"design.json"},"frontier":{"content":{"accepted":true,"blockers":[{"issue":181,"state":"CLOSED"}],"issue":189,"ready":true,"ticket_sha256":"50959c913674f89ffb3c987db66dae89b28eab71b0d68ecb1ec2fb803f8c0937","version":"1.0"},"sha256":"4af569e604a9467d57deea5eb3638a085a72b0eeddbe4f8dd0c98a46e0fcd7d2","source":"frontier.json"},"green-proof":{"content":{"architecture_builder":{"changed_files":["app/frontend/src/__tests__/ChatArea-citation-focus.test.tsx","app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.focus.test.tsx","app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.tsx"],"context_sha256":"674a06476636c493cb59dc93f93505743dff5b622665f990f3e4107dcff7d7fd","contract_sha256":"1e4872c41bedc71ca8e0210062d87b20f0b7c8a12d8843d5ada96bdcef2ef63b","convergence":"improves","debts":[],"design_sha256":"b12a6976956859c6e8671faf313c3183da72f643b7badf40fad1b106dbbacd02","diff_sha256":"449136a99ca64d4d90e412754a60218a28362b9c5afc19a7b1d0e6e069d8c452","findings":[],"governor_sha256":"745fc34fbbb440a293ecd61d49bc36ebc0c0a5a18eda640d9640b9ae15037651","head_sha":"828094ac8b419dc30e25a23fe71fbc805ad36a2a","migrations":[],"policy_sha256":"0db30c9f1e05383df234c84feb31dcef348f09ec605db423606b9f72c7e54add","principles":["ARCH-DEEP-MODULES","ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES"],"rationale":["ARCH-FRONTEND-BOUNDARIES: the new keyboard focus entry/return is UI behavior owned by a presentation component; it lives inside CitationModal's own mount/unmount lifecycle (one ref plus one empty-deps useEffect with cleanup) and does not move or duplicate state/network orchestration that belongs in hooks or lib.","Layer direction is intact: CitationModal.tsx adds no import edges (still only react and the ../lib/api type import), no new npm dependency, no cross-layer shortcut, and its public signature (citation, onClose) is unchanged, so callers need no new props, callbacks or state.","ARCH-DEEP-MODULES: the diff extends the existing CitationModal module in place rather than adding a parallel helper, one-off useFocusReturn hook, or speculative extension point for a single-caller concern, matching the codebase's existing focus-on-open precedent in AddVideoModal and the component's existing empty-deps body-scroll-lock effect pattern.","The empty dependency array is architecturally deliberate: it makes focus entry/return a pure mount/unmount concern immune to onClose identity churn from ChatArea's fresh per-render closures, keeping the capability behind an unchanged and stable interface (a deeper module, not a wider one).","ChatArea.tsx and Message.tsx are untouched by the diff; opener capture and restore were not pushed into the caller, so the no-growth hotspot DEBT-CHAT-AREA is not implicated and MIG-FRONTEND-LARGE-COMPONENTS direction (behavior into focused seams, not enlarging large components) is respected — consistent with the kernel-computed empty migrations and debts sets.","The two new test files add no production seam or abstraction: they are colocated per existing convention (components/ next to CitationModal.test.tsx, __tests__/ next to ChatArea-*.test.tsx) and exercise only public seams — render, unmount, document.activeElement, role/accessible-name queries — including the Escape path through the existing document keydown handler and the detached-opener guard, without pinning implementation internals.","Convergence improves on the multi-ticket horizon: real keyboard-accessibility behavior is added behind an unchanged interface with zero new coupling, and nothing in the diff forecloses a deliberate shared focus seam if a future second or third modal ever justifies extracting one."],"verdict":"conform","version":"1.0"},"architecture_builder_sha256":"a67c660bb8d50b0671438b5bed1b31078212fd54a8a82c24e0fc74e65594f43e","architecture_guard":{"artifact":"/home/runner/work/_temp/dark-factory/runs/issue-189-a1-b2f0c75df2/artifacts/final-green-proof.architecture.json","new_cycles":0,"new_forbidden_edges":0,"no_growth_regressions":0,"sha256":"163d742ffd20f7cd644369bbd1d9bc6b06a6191f823626f5249bc49214b41256","unplanned_product_files":0},"change_impact":{"artifact":"/home/runner/work/_temp/dark-factory/runs/issue-189-a1-b2f0c75df2/artifacts/final-green-proof.impact.json","risk":"high","sha256":"86b0bdc389891c39815b1ab5b1e9006a1432f36bbe26b7bac03c46341141070c"},"checkpoints":[{"acceptance_id":"AC-1","argv":["npx","vitest","run","src/components/CitationModal.focus.test.tsx","-t","AC-1"],"cwd":"app/frontend","expected_failure":"AC-1: focus must move to Close button on mount","files":["app/frontend/src/components/CitationModal.focus.test.tsx"],"kind":"red","red_exit":1,"red_output_sha256":"8007ff015f15664f9161989a062f50136645dc4bad370d74335cf3c5c98d115c","red_output_tail":"<button%0A-   aria-label=\"Close\"%0A-   class=\"bg-none border-none text-slate-400 cursor-pointer text-xl leading-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-[var(--accent)] focus-visible:outline-none\"%0A- >%0A-   ×%0A+ <button>%0A+   opener%0A  </button